---

<span id="glance-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="glance-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="glance-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <h2
      id="glance-section-0"
    >
      Bring another open tab into view.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Choose explicitly</h3><p>
        Press ⌘⇧G on macOS or Ctrl+Shift+G on Windows and Linux, or choose View
        → Open Glance. Pick a tab from the current window; the picker stays
        within its local profile.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Give each page the room it needs</h3><p>
        Drag the divider or resize it with the keyboard. Wide windows put the
        pages side by side; narrow windows stack the reference below the main
        page.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Change, swap, or finish</h3><p>
        Use Change to choose another reference, Make main to swap the two pages,
        or Close to dismiss Glance without closing either tab.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="glance-section-1">
  <div>
    <h2 id="glance-section-1">
      A temporary view for the task in front of you.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Both visible pages stay available</h3><p>
        Selecting a quiet tab for Glance reloads it. While it remains visible as
        your reference, Quiet Tabs leaves it alone.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep the choice local</h3><p>
        The picker uses tabs from this window and profile. It does not search
        history, Favorites, remote tabs, or another window.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="glance-note-title">
  <h2 id="glance-note-title">
    Glance is temporary.
  </h2>
  <p>
    The Glance relationship and divider position are device-local and never
    written to session restore or sync. The underlying ordinary tabs keep their
    usual browsing behavior.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/support#tab-groups"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="glance"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >Keep related tabs in Named Groups <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
  >
</aside>
